reate  now the plan was pitched by blockchain  llc  blockchain said that local governments  were simply inadequate to  properly deal with their innovative  technologies so they wanted to create  their own  semi-autonomous local government within  story county  well i spoke with story county manager  austin austin osborne  about how it all went down the plan was  not to involve story counting  at least the way the draft was drafted  the way it was discussed  what frustration was there from story  county's point of view  on the way things were going the  frustration  some of it is even to this day we were  never provided  what the bill draft review was to look  like  so the best thing we could do as a team  is to work on  what we did have which was some document  that was provided us  in march that was to resemble a bill  draft but we weren't sure exactly you  know if that was going to you know be  what was to be dropped  in the legislature or not where we had a  real problem  was the separatist local government  the idea that for some reason that you  know a county or story county can't keep  up with them you know to move any faster  so that they have to separate into a  completely other government  we opposed very strongly and we met with  legislators and we met with regional  leaders  and talked them about that position and  we met with the group  the proponents as well and said you want  to do  almost all of the things you want to do  technology growth  a residential growth at a try submit an  application  get a 30-day grading permit get a or a  5-day grading permit get a 30-day  building permit  go through the plan unit development  process we'll get you up and running  but don't separate from local government  the separating  uh would be detrimental to story county  what  okay fine they want to do their own  thing why should story county  uh be a part of the process  well you know there's different parts to  it but one is  they want to separate into a separate  